WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.487
This query uses the lateral VALUES pattern and then filters out rows whose generated revenue is NULL.

00:00:06.487 --> 00:00:09.617
The WHERE clause makes the policy explicit.

00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:14.577
Run it and compare the row count with a version that keeps all generated rows.

00:00:14.577 --> 00:00:19.217
Always document whether missing cells were preserved or removed.

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:26.687
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:26.687 --> 00:00:30.172
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:36.202
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.030
combination.
